model {
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "A provider may rotate a refresh token before Home writes the new one back, so a stopping Home must never lose a claimed refresh. Once claimed, the provider call no longer ends when its caller is cancelled; it keeps the refresh's deadline, at most 30 s from the refresh's start. On SIGTERM Home refuses new refreshes, including one that was waiting on its credential's lock, and waits up to 45 s for claimed ones to write back; the supervisor gives Home 60 s before it kills it, and reports a drain that gave up and a kill at that bound as closed records. Home reports its refreshes in flight on the database-free /healthz, which the supervisor copies onto /ready while it is at most 3 s old. A provider rejection that disables a credential is one closed line naming the credential only by an opaque reference."
    }
  }
}
